CORE
main.cpp

^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ inherited: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ inherited through an alias: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
guess_function_template_args took the enclosing class from the call's
ID_C_class (the derived class), so `B...' in the default template argument
was unbound, substitution failed, and `derived<int, char> d(1, 2)' found
no match.  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this program, and it fails only its
WRONG assertion.
